	&lt;li&gt;(add) .travis.yml&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</comment>
                            <comment id="16035019" author="githubbot" created="Fri, 2 Jun 2017 16:42:30 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Github user sijie commented on the issue:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/bookkeeper/pull/168&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/bookkeeper/pull/168&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    @jvrao I am open to move from travis to jenkins. but I think there is value for keep both. the reason I added travis: people can enable travis ci on their folks, so it can use travis ci to verify the build before sending a pull request.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    I haven&apos;t used Circle before. Any ideas on what are the differences? I am not sure if Apache INFRA support circle or not.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
